15:34.159 --> 15:36.962
-Sometimes things just jump
from pocket...
-We need to go!

15:40.798 --> 15:42.833
*

15:47.238 --> 15:49.474
When you piss, do you go
straight through the zipper

15:49.507 --> 15:51.909
or do you go over the boxers?

15:53.244 --> 15:54.712
Over the boxers.

15:54.745 --> 15:57.548
Yeah. Me, too.

15:57.582 --> 16:00.885
But is that the right way,
though?

16:00.918 --> 16:02.320
I don't think so.

16:02.353 --> 16:04.322
Bro, you could...

16:04.355 --> 16:06.057
Yeah.

16:06.091 --> 16:09.027
But, I mean, I do switch it up
when I'm wearing a suit.

16:09.060 --> 16:11.329
You know?

16:13.931 --> 16:16.734
EARN: I didn't even know
this neighborhood existed.

16:16.767 --> 16:19.570
DARIUS:
Mm-hmm. Yeah.

16:19.604 --> 16:21.906
-Yep.

16:21.939 --> 16:24.909
YOUNG MAN: Uh,
we'll help you out down here.

16:24.942 --> 16:27.078
Hey. How can I help you guys?

16:27.112 --> 16:29.747
Yeah, we need
a passport replacement.

16:29.780 --> 16:31.416
-Today.
-Yeah.

16:31.449 --> 16:33.618
Okay. Yeah, yeah, yeah. Um,

16:33.651 --> 16:38.056
just, uh, fill out these forms,
and we can make it happen.

16:38.089 --> 16:39.590
All right. Thank you.
I love you.

16:39.624 --> 16:42.427
Thanks.

16:42.460 --> 16:45.763
Really? 'Cause I-I really
thought we were gonna be S.O.L.

16:45.796 --> 16:48.666
Yeah. It's what we do here.

16:48.699 --> 16:50.435
Y'all, uh, going on tour?

16:50.468 --> 16:52.437
Y'all in a rap entourage?

16:52.470 --> 16:53.671
Manager?

16:53.704 --> 16:56.341
How'd you know?

16:56.374 --> 16:58.176
We kind of have a...

16:58.209 --> 17:00.478
specific clientele here. And...

17:00.511 --> 17:02.080
rappers are procrastinators.

17:02.113 --> 17:03.614
No offense.

17:03.648 --> 17:04.849
None taken.

17:04.882 --> 17:08.086
So, who y'all work with?

17:08.119 --> 17:09.920
Uh, Paper Boi.

17:09.954 --> 17:11.822
We're going on tour
with Clark County in Europe.

17:11.856 --> 17:13.758
Oh, man, that's cool. Nice.

17:13.791 --> 17:16.961
I was just listening
to that new Clark joint.

17:16.994 --> 17:19.630
-* Yoo-hoo. * Yeah, yeah.

17:19.664 --> 17:21.032
Oh, man.

17:21.066 --> 17:23.068
Yo, y'all need
an entertainment lawyer?

17:23.101 --> 17:24.702
My cousin is primo.

17:24.735 --> 17:27.372
Uh, I need ID.

17:27.405 --> 17:29.707
Oh. Yeah.

17:29.740 --> 17:32.310
How'd your cousin
get into the business?

17:32.343 --> 17:34.979
Uh, my uncle does it.

17:35.012 --> 17:37.348
Thanks, man.

17:38.983 --> 17:40.851
Let me ask you something.

17:40.885 --> 17:43.221
And, um,

17:43.254 --> 17:45.723
be honest.

17:45.756 --> 17:47.492
Do you think
there's a black lawyer

17:47.525 --> 17:49.327
who's as good as your cousin?

17:57.902 --> 17:59.870
There definitely is.

17:59.904 --> 18:03.641
But, um, part of being good at
your job are your connections,

18:03.674 --> 18:05.876
and black people
just don't have the connections

18:05.910 --> 18:08.279
that my cousin has.

18:08.313 --> 18:12.283
For systemic reasons.

18:12.317 --> 18:13.684
All right.

18:13.718 --> 18:14.919
It's all good.

18:14.952 --> 18:16.354
Oh, perfect.

18:16.387 --> 18:18.189
Yeah, it should be,
like, uh, two hours.

18:18.223 --> 18:19.524
-Oh.
-Cool.

18:19.557 --> 18:20.791
-That's fast.
-Yeah, yeah.

18:20.825 --> 18:23.328
It's, uh, $350.

18:23.361 --> 18:25.730
Oh, that's why. Okay.

18:25.763 --> 18:27.398
Y'all take RushCards?

18:27.432 --> 18:28.899
Yeah, I think so.

18:33.871 --> 18:36.574
DARIUS:
Here you go, my Jewish friend.

18:36.607 --> 18:39.009
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

18:50.188 --> 18:52.890
How's it going, Earn?

18:52.923 --> 18:55.893
You doing all right?

18:55.926 --> 18:58.929
Definitely not.

19:02.600 --> 19:05.570
Is Al gonna fire me?

19:05.603 --> 19:07.572
I don't know.

19:07.605 --> 19:10.007
Maybe.

19:13.010 --> 19:15.580
I know you're always at peace
with everything,

19:15.613 --> 19:18.983
but my whole world's
falling apart.

19:19.016 --> 19:21.352
So...

19:35.533 --> 19:37.368
Look, man,

19:37.402 --> 19:40.771
Alfred, his whole world
changing up with the quickness.

19:40.805 --> 19:42.773
Everything's moving, but...

19:42.807 --> 19:45.176
he ain't gonna never forget
to take care of the ones

19:45.210 --> 19:47.778
he's supposed to provide for,
including you.

19:47.812 --> 19:49.180
I don't want a handout.

19:49.214 --> 19:50.948
I got to provide, too.

19:50.981 --> 19:52.883
I'm getting better at this.
You know that.

19:52.917 --> 19:54.151
-No, I know.
-You know.

19:54.185 --> 19:57.888
I see you, man.
I see you... learning.

19:57.922 --> 20:01.792
But...
learning requires failure.

20:01.826 --> 20:05.196
Al just trying to make sure
you ain't failing in...

20:05.230 --> 20:07.898
in his life.

20:07.932 --> 20:11.101
You know, like,
y'all both black, so...

20:11.135 --> 20:14.104
I mean, y'all both
can't afford to fail.

20:17.074 --> 20:19.444
Do Nigerians get a chance
to fail?

20:19.477 --> 20:20.911
Hey, don't you start that.

20:20.945 --> 20:22.813
You know Nigerians don't fail.

20:28.753 --> 20:30.921
Look, whatever he does,

20:30.955 --> 20:33.491
he ain't gonna do it
till we get to Europe.

20:33.524 --> 20:36.261
Give you a chance
to see the world.

20:36.294 --> 20:38.629
How do you know?

20:40.731 --> 20:43.468
Seems like an Al thing to do.

20:59.550 --> 21:01.652
Y'all ready to do this?

21:01.686 --> 21:04.955
Yeah. Darius is coming down,

21:04.989 --> 21:07.892
and I'm calling a Lyft
right now.

21:07.925 --> 21:10.561
Don't you got
to take the truck back?

21:11.962 --> 21:14.198
Kenny's gonna do it.

21:14.231 --> 21:16.867
I offered
to pay him ten dollars.

21:25.576 --> 21:27.945
Can we talk?

21:29.580 --> 21:32.016
Let's talk when we land, man.

21:37.555 --> 21:40.291
(Darius imitates
plane engine buzzing)

21:43.861 --> 21:45.730
Boom.

21:50.100 --> 21:51.902
That's all you're bringing?

21:51.936 --> 21:53.704
Oh, yeah.

21:53.738 --> 21:56.073
Yeah, rule number one--
pack like a Navy SEAL.

21:56.106 --> 21:58.275
Only take what you need.

22:01.011 --> 22:04.048
EARN: Lyft'll be here
in three minutes.

22:05.850 --> 22:09.420
(car approaches,
music plays with booming beat)

22:09.454 --> 22:11.822
(car engine
and music playing fade)

22:19.897 --> 22:21.599
No.

22:21.632 --> 22:23.834
Come on. You know you want it.

22:25.636 --> 22:27.438
-EARN: No, I'm all right.
-* Ooh-hoo! *

22:27.472 --> 22:29.540
* Whoo-hoo, whoo-hoo *

22:29.574 --> 22:31.642
* Whoo-hoo, whoo-hoo! *

22:33.010 --> 22:34.979
:
Smoke me!

22:35.012 --> 22:36.614
I really want to be smoked.

22:36.647 --> 22:40.084
: I'm okay.

22:40.117 --> 22:41.586
:
You know you want to smoke me.

22:47.625 --> 22:49.326
: Welcome to
-EARN: Gate C7.

22:49.360 --> 22:51.228
-Atlanta, Hartsfield
International Airport.
-Uh-huh.

22:51.261 --> 22:53.998
See, I told you, Earn.
We was gonna make it.

22:54.031 --> 22:57.001
You just got to learn
to trust yourself, my friend.

22:57.034 --> 22:58.636
We're still late, actually.

22:58.669 --> 23:00.505
She printed our tickets,
but she made sure to say,

23:00.538 --> 23:02.473
"Y'all ain't gonna make it,"
five times

23:02.507 --> 23:05.643
while she was doing it, so we
should probably still hurry.

23:05.676 --> 23:07.612
MAN :
Thank you.

23:07.645 --> 23:09.714
-No, no.

23:11.015 --> 23:12.450
WOMAN :
Elizabeth Battola,

23:12.483 --> 23:13.818
your child is waiting
for you...

23:13.851 --> 23:16.454
CLARK: Oh, shit.
Is that Paper Boi?

23:16.487 --> 23:18.188
What's up, y'all?

23:18.222 --> 23:19.657
-Y'all niggas ready
for this tour?
-Sh... Oh, yeah.

23:19.690 --> 23:21.659
Man, we gonna be poppin' bottles
in Paris, bro.

23:21.692 --> 23:23.093
-It's gonna be crazy. Yeah.
-It's lit, bro.

23:23.127 --> 23:24.429
Speaking sign language to hoes.

23:24.462 --> 23:26.196
-It's gonna be dope, man.

23:26.230 --> 23:27.698
-I'm good, man.
-You check out that lawyer
I sent you?

23:27.732 --> 23:29.133
Hell, yeah, man.
He's perfect. I appreciate it.

23:30.801 --> 23:33.237
Hey, okay, cool.
Let's-let's do this over here.

23:33.270 --> 23:35.673
Flight's not gonna leave
without Clark County, baby.

23:35.706 --> 23:38.709
-Yeah.

23:38.743 --> 23:40.511
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

23:40.545 --> 23:43.213
-WOMAN: Please take liquids

23:43.247 --> 23:45.315
-out of your bags...

23:45.349 --> 23:46.984
...and laptops, too.

23:47.017 --> 23:49.219
Place everything in the bins.

23:49.253 --> 23:52.256
-Your pockets should be empty.
-WOMAN 2: Remove your jackets.

23:52.289 --> 23:54.625
:
Opt out!

23:54.659 --> 23:56.994
-MAN: Oh.

23:57.027 --> 23:59.630
You always got to opt out.
Opt for the pat-down, man.

23:59.664 --> 24:02.366
I'm telling you, this-this thing
here-- bad business.

24:04.068 --> 24:06.003
That's why security stays
so close to the food.

24:06.036 --> 24:09.907
They don't want you to smell
your brain frying in this thing.

24:12.443 --> 24:16.447
-WOMAN: Excuse me. Sorry.

24:16.481 --> 24:19.149
WOMAN 2:
Everything in the bins, people.

24:21.385 --> 24:23.754
(sound ceases
except for quiet beeping)

24:37.902 --> 24:39.470
(sound resumes,
indistinct chatter)

24:39.504 --> 24:41.371
Will you hand me a bin?

24:41.405 --> 24:43.040
You got to get it
from the front, man.

24:43.073 --> 24:45.142
Oh, man, he asked nicely.

24:45.175 --> 24:48.278
-Thanks.

24:48.312 --> 24:50.915
(indistinct,
overlapping crowd chatter)

24:50.948 --> 24:52.717
-ALFRED: You know what
I don't get?

24:52.750 --> 24:55.052
How they make you take all your
shit off, and they try to rush

24:55.085 --> 24:56.887
to get you out of the way,
like they ain't just asked me

24:56.921 --> 24:58.723
-to take all your shit off
ten seconds ago.

24:58.756 --> 24:59.990
ALFRED: That's why I fuckin'
hate the airport, man.

25:00.024 --> 25:01.592
DARIUS:
Yeah, it's not efficient.

25:01.626 --> 25:03.027
-ALFRED: All that shit isn't.
-We should hurry.

25:03.060 --> 25:04.795
-All right.

25:04.829 --> 25:06.296
Hey, what
What's going on?

25:06.330 --> 25:07.698
WOMAN:
We're going this way.

25:07.732 --> 25:08.933
We're starting another line
this way.

25:08.966 --> 25:10.601
CLARK:
Hey, yo, Luke, come here.

25:22.813 --> 25:25.482
Man, this trip
gonna be crazy, boy.

25:25.516 --> 25:30.655
I mean, I ain't never really
left Georgia before, so, yeah.

25:30.688 --> 25:32.790
Yeah.

25:32.823 --> 25:34.925
Yeah, it's gonna be cool.

25:37.394 --> 25:39.630
Yeah, it'll be cool.

25:39.664 --> 25:42.066
-Shit.

25:42.099 --> 25:44.101
Yeah.

25:47.838 --> 25:49.840
-WOMAN 2: Yes, ma'am.

25:49.874 --> 25:52.209
WOMAN: Okay, I'm just gonna
move this over here

25:52.242 --> 25:54.645
to make a little more room.

25:54.679 --> 25:56.947
I saw what you did...

25:56.981 --> 25:59.984
-at TSA.
-Mm.

26:00.017 --> 26:02.452
You ain't got to say shit.

26:06.090 --> 26:09.860
Just know that's exactly
what I'm talking about.

26:13.130 --> 26:16.066
Niggas do not care about us,
man.

26:17.635 --> 26:20.037
Niggas gonna do whatever
they got to do to survive,

26:20.070 --> 26:22.172
'cause they ain't got no choice.

26:23.608 --> 26:25.976
We ain't got no choice, either.

26:30.480 --> 26:32.449
You my family, Earn.

26:34.018 --> 26:37.087
Yeah, you...

26:37.121 --> 26:40.257
You're the only one
that knows what I'm about.

26:42.593 --> 26:44.995
You give a fuck.

26:46.463 --> 26:48.599
I need that.

26:50.901 --> 26:53.303
All right?

27:01.278 --> 27:03.380
All right, then.

27:03.413 --> 27:05.515
Hey?

27:05.549 --> 27:07.417
Let's get this money.

27:08.919 --> 27:10.287
BOTH:
Brrr!

27:10.320 --> 27:11.722
-Hey, shit.
-Yeah, boy.

27:16.026 --> 27:18.462
ALFRED:
Hey, Clark, man?

27:19.964 --> 27:22.232
Let me holler at you.

27:22.266 --> 27:24.134
Yeah. What's up, man?

27:24.168 --> 27:25.903
Where Luke at, man?

27:25.936 --> 27:27.838
Uh, nah, man.

27:27.872 --> 27:30.040
Luke got in some shit.
Cops took him.

27:30.074 --> 27:32.710
ALFRED:
What you talking about?

27:32.743 --> 27:36.046
TSA found a tool in his bag.

27:36.080 --> 27:37.581
Damn.

27:37.614 --> 27:39.183
-Oh.
-It's just kind of...

27:39.216 --> 27:40.584
Oh, he probably had
a screwdriver or something.

27:40.617 --> 27:41.919
You can't have those on a plane.

27:41.952 --> 27:44.488
Yeah. More like a hammer.

27:44.521 --> 27:45.956
Yeah. It was gold, too.

27:47.692 --> 27:49.226
Shit was clean, though.

27:49.259 --> 27:50.928
Wish it was mine.

27:50.961 --> 27:53.630
* Yoohoo! *

28:01.305 --> 28:03.741
The piece was in Clark's bag.

28:13.417 --> 28:15.820
-*

28:22.192 --> 28:24.161
-TRACY: Yo, Alf!

28:24.194 --> 28:25.963
Yo, open the door, man!

28:30.400 --> 28:33.070
Open up, man!

28:33.103 --> 28:36.841
Listen, man, I got Chinese food
with a side of chocolate.

28:36.874 --> 28:39.609
!

28:39.643 --> 28:43.080
Is this mother...?
Al, man,

28:43.113 --> 28:44.648
-stop playing, bro. Let me in!
-WOMAN: Shut the fuck up!

28:44.681 --> 28:47.317
Hey, you shut the fuck up!
The hell you talking to?

28:47.351 --> 28:50.687
-Ready to whoop your ass.

28:50.721 --> 28:52.957
-Hey! Wake up, niggas!
-* So I remember everything *

28:52.990 --> 28:55.192
Alfred, will you open
the goddamn door?!

28:57.561 --> 28:59.363
-* Of every man *
-* Ooh, ooh *

28:59.396 --> 29:01.832
* Who put me here *

29:03.033 --> 29:04.634
* Oh-oh *

29:04.668 --> 29:10.707
* I see my light come shining *

29:14.044 --> 29:16.346
* From the west down *

29:16.380 --> 29:21.919
* To the east... *

29:21.952 --> 29:26.723
* Any day, now *

29:26.757 --> 29:31.261
* Any day,
now *

29:31.295 --> 29:37.067
* I shall be released *

29:41.872 --> 29:45.075
* They say every man needs
protection *

29:49.413 --> 29:53.784
* They say
every man must fall. *

29:59.056 --> 30:01.591
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
